-- Estimated entries from off-app bank transfers, imported from final.csv.
--
-- The transfers listed there never made it into the database (no
-- payment.fio.unmatched audit row, no `recordEstimatedEntry` call), so the
-- statistics had no way to know the visits happened. This seeds
-- `EstimatedEntry` for them directly.
--
-- The `entries` numbers are not guessed here by hand: they are exactly what
-- the app's own estimator (`estimateEntriesForAmount` in
-- src/lib/payment-entry-estimate.ts) returns for each amount against the
-- *production* price list of single entries at the time this file was
-- generated — 100 Kč (Dítě do 15 let), 125 Kč (Student/Senior), 150 Kč (Dospělý).
--
-- One row per transfer (423 of them, 711 entries in total).
-- The CSV carries only a date, no Fio transaction id, so `fioIdPohyb` is a
-- synthetic `import-<date>-<n>` key: unique, and clearly not a real Fio id.
-- `createdAt` is that date at noon UTC — the same Prague calendar day, which
-- is all the charts bucket by.
--
-- `INSERT OR IGNORE` on the unique `fioIdPohyb` index keeps this re-runnable.
-- Caveat: a transfer in here that Fio later reports again under its real id
-- would be recorded a second time — there is no key to tie the two together.

